{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{U \\times_X X_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-recognize-fpqc-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:99400a8489ad9b3c9339628f6f2357b9a681b0d367973c99a5bb6743f7efe38f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8bb61279bb60495fd6d65a2c747deb161db7cef38a1987a464778e0751843fdc", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0004> is a family of morphisms of\nalgebraic spaces with target <MATH_0005>. Let <MATH_0006> be a surjective\n<ACCENT_0001>tale morphism from a scheme towards <MATH_0007>. Then\n<MATH_0008> is an fpqc covering of <MATH_0009> if and only\nif <MATH_0010> is an fpqc covering of <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5516d4c8a165005db3edd572d025b2e88992e03c9e2c7901695dd5e02c85de0f", "unit_id": "tag:03MS:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{U \\times_X X_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{U \\times_X X_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$h : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\times_X Z \\to Z$", "MATH_0007": "$W_1, \\ldots, W_t$", "MATH_0008": "$U \\times_X Z$", "MATH_0009": "$Z$", "MATH_0010": "$j$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{U \\times_X X_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$W_j \\to U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{W_{jl} \\to W_j\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\{W_j \\times_X X_i \\to W_j\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{W_{jl} \\to Z\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$Z$", "MATH_0017": "$\\{Z \\times_X X_i \\to X\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fpqc}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-lemma-fpqc-affine-axioms}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a8ed1ac3118eb810c243e0ee43701700c9833a5c9d868b93a30921f8c939dea8", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ce72fa87631c8d09a3367605a26ab0e83a0df9a23b5ee785ae5ba7918ff39a4d", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is an fpqc covering, then so is\n<MATH_0002> by Lemma <REF_0001>.\nAssume that <MATH_0003> is an fpqc covering.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a morphism from an affine scheme towards <MATH_0005>.\nThen we see that <MATH_0006> is a surjective <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\nof schemes, in particular open. Hence we can find finitely many affine opens\n<MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008> whose images cover <MATH_0009>.\nFor each <MATH_0010> we may apply the condition that\n<MATH_0011> is an fpqc covering\nto the morphism <MATH_0012>, and obtain a standard fpqc covering\n<MATH_0013> which refines <MATH_0014>.\nHence <MATH_0015> is a standard fpqc covering of <MATH_0016>\n(see\nTopologies, Lemma <REF_0002>)\nwhich refines <MATH_0017> and we win.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e36df281e8e4cae636e0f145da558976c22b089229822e0311f8b35e341228d2", "unit_id": "tag:03MS:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03MP", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{g_i : T_i \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0008": "$T_i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-fpqc-schemes}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7056d68bc16be1ff3e395e12f41cd985f28b987764b01f517f281e2565ad1b27", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa1be04864768db5dc32c0a5ccf6c1b36b393e60cb8cf6f0988d9db870a5157a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0004> is an\nfpqc covering of <MATH_0005>. Then there exists a refinement\n<MATH_0006> of <MATH_0007> which is an\nfpqc covering such that each <MATH_0008> is a scheme.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:374bbbbe3eab933233ef3c3bf813c59977818ebae96dd53d131830cb32b1ecef", "unit_id": "tag:0419:statement"}
